<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is LLP Agreement Change?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>LLP agreement change is the formal amendment of the foundational document governing a Limited Liability Partnership under Section 23 of the LLP Act, 2008. The amendment is documented through a Supplementary LLP Agreement (supplementary deed) &ndash; an addendum that records clauses being amended, new terms, and effective date.</p>
                    <p>The supplementary deed must be on non-judicial stamp paper (Maharashtra Stamp Act value), signed by all partners, witnessed by 2 persons. Filed with ROC via Form 3 within 30 days. For business objects changes, Form 3 is approval-based &ndash; ROC reviews before approving. Late filing: Rs 100/day penalty with no cap. For new LLPs, see <a href="/llp-incorporation">LLP Registration</a>.</p>
                    <p>Some amendments require linked filings: Form 4 (partner changes), Form 15 (registered office), Form 5 (name change). For foreign partner amendments, FEMA compliance (LLP-I/LLP-II) is additionally required. See <a href="/fdi-compliance">FDI Compliance</a>.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for LLP Agreement Change:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Section 23:</strong> LLP Act &ndash; any change in agreement must be filed with ROC</li>
                        <li><strong>Form 3:</strong> MCA form for LLP Agreement and changes &ndash; within 30 days, approval-based for objects</li>
                        <li><strong>Supplementary Deed:</strong> Legal document amending the agreement &ndash; stamp paper, all partners, 2 witnesses</li>
                        <li><strong>Form 4:</strong> Partner admission/retirement &ndash; within 30 days alongside Form 3</li>
                        <li><strong>First Schedule:</strong> LLP Act default provisions &ndash; applies when no written agreement exists</li>
                        <li><strong>Approval-Based:</strong> Business objects change requires ROC review and approval before commencement</li>
                    </ul>

                </div>
            </div>
