                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Which ROC handles LLP agreement change in Mumbai?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>ROC Mumbai at Everest House, 100 Marine Lines processes Form 3, Form 4, Form 15, and Form 5 on MCA V3 portal. For business objects changes, ROC reviews and approves. Patron's Marine Lines office adjacent to ROC for direct coordination and query resolution.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is Form 3 and when must it be filed?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>MCA form for LLP Agreement and changes. Within 30 days of amendment. Late filing: Rs 100/day with no cap. For business objects: approval-based (ROC reviews 10-30 days before approving). Other amendments: auto-approved upon filing. Patron files within 15 days for Mumbai LLPs.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Do all partners need to agree?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Generally yes &ndash; all partners must consent unless existing agreement specifies different mechanism (e.g., majority for certain changes). Without specific provision, unanimous consent required under First Schedule. Patron reviews existing agreement's amendment provisions before initiating.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is a supplementary LLP agreement?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Legal document recording the amendment &ndash; specifies clauses changed, new terms replacing old, effective date, partner consent. On Maharashtra non-judicial stamp paper (Rs 100-500 residual), signed by all partners, witnessed by 2 persons. Becomes part of original agreement. Patron drafts for all types.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Is stamp duty required in Mumbai?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. Supplementary deed on non-judicial stamp paper per Maharashtra Stamp Act. General amendments: Rs 100-500 (residual entry). Financial amendments (capital, significant monetary): may be higher based on value. Patron determines correct Maharashtra stamp duty for every amendment to prevent insufficiency.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can business objects be changed?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. Amend objects clause in supplementary deed, file Form 3. Important: approval-based &ndash; ROC reviews and may request additional documents. LLP cannot commence new activity until ROC approves. Processing: 10-30 days. Patron manages the approval process and ROC follow-up for Mumbai LLPs.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-7">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is the penalty for late Form 3?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Rs 100 per day with NO cap. Starts from 31st day after amendment. 6 months: Rs 18,000. 1 year: Rs 36,500. Non-filing also creates MCA compliance gap that may block other filings (Form 8, Form 11). Patron files within 15 days to prevent all penalties for Mumbai LLPs.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-8">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can multiple amendments be combined?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. Multiple simultaneous changes can be combined in single supplementary deed and single Form 3. If different effective dates needed: separate filings required. Patron advises Mumbai LLPs on bundling vs separate filings based on efficiency and effective date requirements.</p></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>


